      "tips": [
        {
          "text": "Practice aptitude questions on IndiaBix and refer to the “1000 Sanfoundry MCQs” focused on OOPs and Java.",
          "category": "OA preparation",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Ensure fundamentals in JavaScript and SQL are clear, as questions from these areas are commonly asked.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Have complete clarity about your projects—know every detail thoroughly.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Only mention technologies or features on your resume that you have actually worked on.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Maintain confidence, good body language, composure, and wear a smile throughout the interview process.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "If you realize an answer is incorrect, acknowledge it politely and assure the interviewer you will work on it.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Treat the interview as a win‑win situation to gain experience even if you don’t get placed.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Never lose hope; one chance can break through and lead to placement.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Never underestimate yourself; patience and staying calm are key during placement season.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Stay motivated and talk to someone if you feel overwhelmed or stressed.",
